# A chain of leaks: removing the empty line would expose the next one.
-- input.cnf --
[mydumper]
# see [docs]

[

routines=1
-- fixed.cnf --
[mydumper]
# see [docs]
#
[

routines=1
-- diagnostics --
3:1-3:1 error MDL108[bracket-state-leak] mydumper's pre-processor turns this empty line into `= 1` because line 2 contains `[` after other text (GLib: Key file contains line “= 1” which is not a key-value pair, group, or comment)
  = mydumper ignores this entire file: it only logs a WARNING ("Failed to load config file") and runs with its defaults, exit code 0.
  note 2:1-2:13: mydumper's pre-processor does not reset its state after this line, because it contains `[`
  fix (safe): Turn the empty line into a `#` line, which stops the leak
